{"format":"vecta/0.1","id":"area-of-a-circle","title":"Area of a circle","subject":"Maths","level":"Ages 11-14","language":"en","voice":"recorded","duration":48.66,"board":{"aspect":"16:9"},"audio":[{"src":"voice.opus","type":"audio/ogg; codecs=opus"},{"src":"voice.m4a","type":"audio/mp4"}],"captions":[{"t":0.25,"text":"Today, we're going to find the area of a circle."},{"t":3.0,"text":"Here is a circle. The point in the middle is called the center."},{"t":6.41,"text":"The distance from the center to the edge is called the radius. We call it r."},{"t":11.02,"text":"The area is the amount of space inside the circle."},{"t":13.95,"text":"To find it, we use this formula. A equals pi r squared."},{"t":18.11,"text":"Pi is a special number. It is about three point one four."},{"t":21.91,"text":"Let's try an example. Suppose the radius is three centimetres."},{"t":26.02,"text":"We put three into the formula. A equals pi, times three squared."},{"t":30.77,"text":"Three squared is nine. So A equals nine pi."},{"t":34.21,"text":"Nine times three point one four is about twenty eight point three."},{"t":38.49,"text":"So the area is about twenty eight point three square centimetres."},{"t":42.4,"text":"Remember. A equals pi r squared. Square the radius first, then multiply by pi."}],"elements":[{"t":0.39,"type":"text","value":"Area of a circle","x":50,"y":12,"size":8,"weight":700},{"t":3.22,"type":"circle","x":30,"y":55,"r":26,"dur":1.2},{"t":4.76,"type":"dot","x":30,"y":55},{"t":4.9,"type":"text","value":"center","x":30,"y":62,"size":4.5,"color":"muted"},{"t":7.14,"type":"line","x1":30,"y1":55,"x2":44.6,"y2":55,"color":"accent","dur":0.8},{"t":9.67,"type":"text","value":"r","x":37.3,"y":50,"size":6,"color":"accent","italic":true},{"t":11.32,"type":"fill","x":30,"y":55,"r":26,"color":"accent"},{"t":14.81,"type":"math","value":"A = \\pi r^2","x":72,"y":42,"size":9},{"t":18.75,"type":"math","value":"\\pi \\approx 3.14","x":72,"y":62,"size":6,"color":"muted"},{"t":21.91,"type":"clear"},{"t":22.06,"type":"text","value":"Example","x":50,"y":12,"size":8,"weight":700},{"t":22.37,"type":"circle","x":22,"y":55,"r":20,"dur":1.0},{"t":23.28,"type":"dot","x":22,"y":55},{"t":23.58,"type":"line","x1":22,"y1":55,"x2":33.25,"y2":55,"color":"accent","dur":0.6},{"t":24.04,"type":"text","value":"r = 3 cm","x":26.5,"y":61,"size":4,"color":"accent"},{"t":26.25,"type":"math","value":"A = \\pi r^2","x":66,"y":30,"size":6},{"t":27.69,"type":"math","value":"A = \\pi \\times 3^2","x":66,"y":44,"size":6},{"t":31.82,"type":"math","value":"A = 9\\pi","x":66,"y":58,"size":6},{"t":34.55,"type":"math","value":"A \\approx 9 \\times 3.14","x":66,"y":72,"size":6},{"t":38.96,"type":"math","value":"A \\approx 28.3\\ \\text{cm}^2","x":66,"y":87,"size":6.5,"color":"accent","box":true},{"t":42.4,"type":"clear"},{"t":42.58,"type":"text","value":"Remember","x":50,"y":18,"size":8,"weight":700},{"t":43.28,"type":"math","value":"A = \\pi r^2","x":50,"y":45,"size":12,"color":"accent","box":true},{"t":45.55,"type":"text","value":"1. Square the radius","x":50,"y":70,"size":5},{"t":46.95,"type":"text","value":"2. Multiply by π","x":50,"y":80,"size":5}]}